ce \u8226\'20\'22 Stops above 146.00 taken out, any option barriers at 146.00 history \u8226\'20\'22 Upside limited on profit-taking by longs, Japanese exporter staggered offers \u8226\'20\'22 Despite some concerns, no \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , only more official jaw-boning \u8226\'20\'22 FinMin Suzuki says speed of JPY declines issue, USD bias to remain up \u8226\'20\'22 Higher US yields on hawkish Fed expectations to continue to fuel up-move \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY on higher plane, support from @145.50, low today 145.60 \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  10s indicated @3.934%, 2s @4.291%, Nikkei holding around par \u8226\'20\'22 JPY crosses steady, EUR/JPY 141.35-82 EBS, GBP/JPY 159.69-160.40 \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/JPY 91.22-57, AUD/JPY and GBP/JPY downsides over? Jury still out EUR/USD-Edges lower after USD/JPY jumps above 146.00 \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD opened unchanged around 0.9705 after rally stalled at 0.9774 \u8226\'20\'22 BOE comments indicating they will stops supporting Gilts sent USD higher \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD fell to 0.9683 in Asia when the USD/JPY jumped above 146.00 \u8226\'20\'22 Heading into the afternoon the EUR/USD was settled around 0.9695 \u8226\'20\'22 Talk of large option strikes around 0.9700 hemming in price action \u8226\'20\'22 Support is at yesterday's 0.9670 low and the trend low at 0.9528 \u8226\'20\'22 Resistance is at the 10-day MA at 0.9794 and break would ease the pressure \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD in down-trend while key trend-line (1.0019) caps rallies \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD may consolidate ahead of key US CPI on Thursday AUD/USD-Hits fresh 2-year low as down-trend continues \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD opened -0.4% at 0.6273 after falling in NY afternoon following BOE comments \u8226\'20\'22 It came under pressure early when USD/JPY popped above 146.00 \u8226\'20\'22 Selling continued, as AUD took the brunt of USD buying in Asia \u8226\'20\'22 A 3% fall in Dalian iron ore added weight and it fell to 0.6239 \u8226\'20\'22 Buyers finally emerged and AUD/USD settled around 0.6250 into the afternoon \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD trending lower with the 5,10 & 21-day MAs in a bearish formation \u8226\'20\'22 A break above the 10-day MA at 0.6401 is needed to ease downward pressure \u8226\'20\'22 The objective of the trend is the 76.4 of the 2020 low/high at 0.6099 GBP/USD-Pops on \uc2 BoE\uc2  hint bond-buying may be extended \u8226\'20\'22 GBP/USD pops to 1.1060 from early 1.0925 low, up 1.2% on \uc2 BoE\uc2  hint \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 BoE\uc2  signals to lenders it is prepared to extend bond purchases - FT \u8226\'20\'22 Follows \uc2 BoE\uc2  governor saying late Tuesday it would end on Friday \u8226\'20\'22 Potential extension of market relief measures lifts mood \u8226\'20\'22 But technical resistance at 38.2% Fibo 1.1070 obstructs rally \u8226\'20\'22 Bollinger downtrend channel reinstated on close below 1.0920 \u8226\'20\'22 GDP leads UK data - poll flat m/m +2.4% y/y, IP poll -0.2% m/m +0.6% y/y Unless something gives, sterling can slide to parity The risk of a real meltdown in UK markets is intensifying and sterling could potentially drop to parity against the U.S. dollar unless the new government compromises on its tax cut plans. Sterling fell 0.8% on Tuesday, after the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  governor said British pension funds and other investors hit by the recent slump in bond prices had just three days left to fix their problems before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would withdraw support. Gilt yields climbed for the sixth day; the 30-year rose nine basis points to 4.804%, up 96 bps from its 3.842% October open. 0#BOEWATCH prices a 97.65% chance of a 100 bps hike on Nov 3. As fuel and food prices surge, creating a cost-of-living crisis, soaring yields will add fuel to the fire. A deep UK recession and a very tough winter loom. The government's response to the situation shows no sense of urgency. The Financial Times reports a Downing Street spokesperson said on Tuesday "The prime minister remains confident that the measures set out will deliver growth in the UK economy," and the \uc2 BoE\uc2  measures "will support an orderly end to the \uc2 BoE\uc2 's temporary purchase scheme". The \uc2 IMF\uc2  has urged the UK to align fiscal policy with \uc2 BoE\uc2  inflation goals - matching market expectations. GBP/USD charts are turning negative as 21-day Bollinger bands, momentum studies, 5 and 21-day moving averages all head lower. Tuesday's close below 1.1047, 38.2% of the September-October rise, targets 1.0772, the 61.8% retracement. Yuan bears keen to challenge \uc2 PBOC\uc2 , risking backlash Beijing might act more forcefully if warnings of betting against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to be ignored. Despite recent \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  stabilisation measures, consensus bearish bets persist. Last month's reintroduction of the reserve ratio requirement on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  forwards took effect Sept 28 - yet USD/CNY hit a 14-year peak of 7.2521 the same day. \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  has likely been deploying state banks to sell USD in the market to cushion the CNY, but has stopped short of aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unlike the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Policymakers have other ways to defend the yuan, and it appears increasingly likely they will dig into their toolbox soon, with market stability a concern ahead of the Chinese Communist Party's congress beginning Saturday. USD/CNY is again challenging the 7.2000 psychological barrier. While China has no 'line-in-the-sand' for the value of the yuan, and its economy could arguably benefit from a cheaper \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the speed of the move may be a concern if it breaks below last month's trough. The consensus bearish view on the yuan will likely be fortified by upcoming U.S. inflation data, which should affirm USD bulls' conviction that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  is far from done with rate hikes. Chinese trade data due Friday might add fuel to the flames.\par \par \uc2 To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-15T04:57:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221012eiac00kix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
