\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar soars to new 24-year high versus yen; sterling rebounds\b0\par\par\uc2 1,001 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2022\par 21:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds comment, Fed minutes, updates prices)\par \par         * \par       Yen 3-month implied volatility at 11.9, vs 13.26 on Sept. 22\par     \par \par         * \par       Japan watching volatility, not specific levels, analyst says\par     \par \par         * \par       BoE signals to private group it may extend bond buys, FT says\par     \par \par         * \par       U.S. producer prices rise in September\par     \par \par         * \par       Fed minutes had dovish elements\par     \par \par   \par     By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par        NEW YORK, Oct 12 (Reuters) - The dollar climbed to a fresh 24-year peak versus the yen on Wednesday,\par holding above levels that prompted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese officials last month, while sterling rose after\par a sharp fall in the previous session as investors pondered the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2 's next steps.\par     The greenback pared gains after minutes from the last \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  meeting showed some dovish\par undertones. Several participants noted the importance of calibrating the pace of further tightening to\par mitigate the risk on the U.S. economy, the minutes said. The Fed though remained committed to raising\par interest rates in order to bring down inflation.\par         "Maybe there is a bit of hope within the minutes that basically officials are weighing the risk of\par going too hard or going too high on hiking," said Juan Perez, director of trading at Monex USA in\par Washington. \par   \par         "That's not the number one concern right now. Number one concern continues to be inflation." \par   \par     The pound, on the other hand, rose following a drop to a two-week low versus the dollar and euro late on\par Tuesday, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Times\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported that the BoE has signaled privately to lenders it is prepared to\par prolong its bond purchases.\par     Data showing U.S. producer prices increased more than expected in September, further boosted the dollar\par against the yen. The producer price index for final demand rebounded 0.4%, above the forecast for a 0.2%\par rise. In the 12 months through September, the PPI increased 8.5% after advancing 8.7% in August.\par \par     In the wake of the U.S. PPI data, the greenback rose as high as 146.98 yen, its strongest\par since August 1998. It was last up 0.7% at 146.85, marking a fifth straight session of gains.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  staged its first yen-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since 1998 on Sept. 22, when the dollar was at 145.90\par yen. \par     "This just reaffirmed that the BoJ (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) did not defend a particular level, but was addressing\par volatility," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marc Chandler\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief market strategist, at Bannockburn Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in New York, adding\par that the three-month yen volatility was lower on Wednesday than when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month.\par     Three-month implied volatility on the yen was 11.9% , compared with a high of 13.26% on Sept.\par 22 when Japan stepped in to prop up the Japanese unit. \par     Officials have reiterated they stand ready to take appropriate steps to counter excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par moves, though whether they wish to defend particular levels is less clear. \par     Yields outside Japan have been pushed higher by spillover from the turmoil in Britain's bond market. \par     Long-dated gilt yields jumped again, with the 20-year hitting a 14-year high a day after BoE\par Governor Andrew Bailey reiterated late Tuesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would end its emergency bond-buying\par programme on Friday, telling pension fund managers to finish rebalancing their positions by then.\par     Sterling fell to a two week low of $1.0925 after Bailey's remarks, which were reiterated by a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spokesperson on Wednesday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later rebounded to stand 1.2% higher at $1.1083, after\par the FT report which said the BoE had suggested to private lenders that it was open to extending its bond\par purchases.\par     Against the euro, the pound gained. In afternoon trading, the euro was down 1.2% at 87.40 pence\par .\par     Elsewhere, the euro remained under pressure, down 0.1% at $0.9696. \par     The risk-sensitive Australian dollar sank to a 2 1/2-year low of US$0.6236, and was last flat\par at US$0.6274.\par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 3:12PM (1912 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 113.2800       113.3400    -0.04%         18.416%       +113.5900   +113.0200\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9699        $0.9706     -0.07%         -14.68%       +$0.9735    +$0.9668\par  Dollar/Yen                   146.8800       145.8650    +0.73%       