\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. dollar soars to new 24-year high versus yen; sterling rebounds\b0\par\par\uc2 943 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2022\par 21:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The dollar climbed to a fresh 24-year peak versus the yen on Wednesday, holding above levels that prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese officials last month, while sterling rose after a sharp fall in the previous session as investors pondered the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 's next steps.\par \par \uc2 The greenback pared gains after minutes from the last \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  meeting showed some dovish undertones. Several participants noted the importance of calibrating the pace of further tightening to mitigate the risk on the U.S. economy, the minutes said. The Fed though remained committed to raising interest rates in order to bring down inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Maybe there is a bit of hope within the minutes that basically officials are weighing the risk of going too hard or going too high on hiking," said Juan Perez, director of trading at Monex USA in Washington.\par \par \uc2 "That's not the number one concern right now. Number one concern continues to be inflation."\par \par \uc2 The pound, on the other hand, rose following a drop to a two-week low versus the dollar and euro late on Tuesday, after the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  reported that the \uc2 BoE\uc2  has signaled privately to lenders it is prepared to prolong its bond purchases.\par \par \uc2 Data showing U.S. producer prices increased more than expected in September, further boosted the dollar against the yen. The producer price index for final demand rebounded 0.4%, above the forecast for a 0.2% rise. In the 12 months through September, the PPI increased 8.5% after advancing 8.7% in August.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the U.S. PPI data, the greenback rose as high as 146.98 yen, its strongest since August 1998. It was last up 0.7% at 146.85, marking a fifth straight session of gains.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  staged its first yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998 on Sept. 22, when the dollar was at 145.90 yen.\par \par \uc2 "This just reaffirmed that the BoJ (\uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 ) did not defend a particular level, but was addressing volatility," said \uc2 Marc Chandler\uc2 , chief market strategist, at Bannockburn Global \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York, adding that the three-month yen volatility was lower on Wednesday than when \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 Three-month implied volatility on the yen was 11.9% , compared with a high of 13.26% on Sept. 22 when Japan stepped in to prop up the Japanese unit.\par \par \uc2 Officials have reiterated they stand ready to take appropriate steps to counter excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, though whether they wish to defend particular levels is less clear.\par \par \uc2 Yields outside Japan have been pushed higher by spillover from the turmoil in Britain's bond market.\par \par \uc2 Long-dated gilt yields jumped again, with the 20-year hitting a 14-year high a day after \uc2 BoE\uc2  Governor Andrew Bailey reiterated late Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would end its emergency bond-buying programme on Friday, telling pension fund managers to finish rebalancing their positions by then.[GB/]\par \par \uc2 Sterling fell to a two week low of $1.0925 after Bailey's remarks, which were reiterated by a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesperson on Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later rebounded to stand 1.2% higher at $1.1083, after the FT report which said the \uc2 BoE\uc2  had suggested to private lenders that it was open to extending its bond purchases.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the pound gained. In afternoon trading, the euro was down 1.2% at 87.40 pence.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the euro remained under pressure, down 0.1% at $0.9696.\par \par \uc2 The risk-sensitive Australian dollar sank to a 2 1/2-year low of US$0.6236, and was last flat at US$0.6274.\par \par \uc2 ========================================================\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 3:12PM (1912 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Description RIC Last U.S. Close Pct Change YTD Pct High Bid Low Bid\par \par \uc2 Previous Change\par \par \uc2 Session\par \par \uc2 Dollar index 113.2800 113.3400 -0.04% 18.416% +113.5900 +113.0200\par \par \uc2 Euro/Dollar $0.9699 $0.9706 -0.07% -14.68% +$0.9735 +$0.9668\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Yen 146.8800 145.8650 +0.73% +27.63% +146.9550 +145.6000\par \par \uc2 Euro/Yen 142.47 141.58 +0.63% +9.32% +142.6300 +141.4500\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Swiss 0.9978 0.9959 +0.23% +9.43% +1.0004 +0.9932\par \par \uc2 Sterling/Dollar $1.1092 $1.0961 +1.22% -17.96% +$1.1132 +$1.0925\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Canadian 1.3812 1.3795 +0.13% +9.25% +1.3830 +1.3762\par \par \uc2 Aussie/Dollar $0.6274 $0.6273 +0.03% -13.67% +$0.6298 +$0.6236\par \par \uc2 Euro/Swiss 0.9678 0.9677 +0.01% -6.66% +0.9690 +0.9644\par \par \uc2 Euro/Sterling 0.8744 0.8847 -1.16% +4.10% +0.8867 +0.8729\par \par \uc2 NZ $0.5604 $0.5582 +0.42% -18.10% +$0.5632 +$0.5561\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Dollar\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Norway 10.7725 10.7445 +0.14% +22.14% +10.7980 +10.6415\par \par \uc2 Euro/Norway 10.4468 10.4347 +0.12% +4.33% +10.4696 +10.3665\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Sweden 11.3402 11.3577 -0.19% +25.75% +11.3961 +11.3051\par \par \uc2 Euro/Sweden 10.9994 11.0203 -0.19% +7.43% +11.0385 +10.9822\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss; Additional reporting by Amruta Khandekar in Bengalaru, Alun John in London, Kevin Buckland in Tokyo, Georgina Lee in Hong Kong, and Vidya Ranganathan in Singapore; Editing by Paul Simao and Nick Zieminski) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-12T19:54:37.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221012eiac0083p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
