\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar surges to new 24-year high versus yen; sterling rallies\b0\par\par\uc2 1,081 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2022\par 17:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds new comment, U.S. data, byline, NEW YORK dateline, bullets, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  table; updates prices)\par \par         * \par       Yen 3-month implied volatility at 11.9, vs 13.26 on Sept. 22\par     \par \par         * \par       Japan watching volatility, not specific levels, analyst says\par     \par \par         * \par       BoE signals to private group it may extend bond buys, FT says\par     \par \par         * \par       U.S. producer prices rise in September\par     \par \par   \par     By Alun John and Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par        LONDON/NEW YORK, Oct 12 (Reuters) - \par     The dollar climbed to a fresh 24-year peak versus the yen on Wednesday, holding above levels that\par prompted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese officials last month, while sterling rose after a sharp fall in the\par previous session as investors pondered the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2 's next steps.\par   \par         The pound gained following a drop to a two-week low versus the dollar and euro late on Tuesday,\par after the \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Times\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported\par      that the BoE has signalled privately to lenders that it is prepared to prolong its bond purchases.\par   \par         Additional media reports suggested the \f28 \uc2 \f2 UK government\f28 \uc2 \f2  could make a U-turn on more elements of its\par recent "minibudget" that roiled markets.\par   \par     Data showing U.S. producer prices increased more than expected in September, further boosted the dollar\par against the yen. The producer price index for final demand rebounded 0.4%, above the forecast for a 0.2%\par rise. In the 12 months through September, the PPI increased 8.5% after advancing 8.7% in August.\par         Following the U.S. PPI data, the greenback rose as high as 146.88 yen, its strongest level\par since August 1998. It was last up 0.7% at 146.84, marking a fifth straight session of gains.\par   \par     Japanese authorities staged their first yen-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since 1998 on Sept. 22, when the dollar\par was at 145.90 yen. \par         "This just reaffirmed that the BoJ (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) did not defend a particular level, but was\par addressing volatility," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marc Chandler\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief market strategist, at Bannockburn Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in New\par York, adding that three-month yen volatility was lower on Wednesday than when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last month.\par   \par         Three-month implied volatility on the yen was at 11.9% , compared with a high of 13.26% on\par Sept. 22 when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in to prop up the Japanese unit. \par   \par         "Not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the old level was tactically smart. It's like not waving a red flag in front of\par the market. There could be another bout of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but it would have less effect than the first bout,"\par he added.\par   \par     Officials have reiterated they stand ready to take appropriate steps to counter excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par moves, though whether they wish to defend particular levels is less clear. \par     The yen is particularly sensitive to the gap between U.S. and Japanese long-term government bond yields.\par The benchmark 10-year Treasury yield is trading not far from 14-year highs just above 4%, while\par the equivalent Japanese yield is pinned near zero. \par     Yields outside Japan have been pushed higher by spillover from the turmoil in Britain's bond market. \par     Long-dated gilt yields jumped again, with the 20-year hitting a 14-year high a day after BoE\par Governor Andrew Bailey reiterated late on Tuesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would end its emergency bond-buying\par programme on Friday, telling pension fund managers to finish rebalancing their positions by then.\par     Sterling fell to a two week low of $1.0925 after Bailey's remarks, which were reiterated by a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spokesperson on Wednesday. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later rebounded to stand 0.8% higher at $1.1044, after\par the FT report that the BoE had suggested to private lenders that it was open to extending its bond\par purchases.\par         Against the euro, the pound gained. In late morning trading, the euro was down 0.9% at 87.71 pence\par .\par   \par         "What this reflects is that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  and other officials as well like to talk to private\par groups," said Bannockburn's Chandler. "These comments should be made public. By talking to private people,\par they give them information that they don't give to the public."\par   \par     Data earlier in the session showed Britain's economy shrank by 0.3% in August, hit by weakness in\par manufacturing and maintenance work in North Sea oil and gas fields. \par     Elsewhere, the euro remained under pressure, down 0.2% at $0.9686. \par     The risk-sensitive Australian dollar sank to a 2 1/2-year low of US$0.6236, and was last flat\par on the day at US$0.6268.\par     ===================================================