\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Japan's foreign reserves drop by record on market shakeout,  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 742 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2022\par 11:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  foreign reserves down for two straight months\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $1.238 trillion reserves second largest after China\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Drop in reserves comes after last month's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Authorities mum on speculation about selling U.S. Treasuries\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Never felt limit to "ammunitions" for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - Kanda\par \par \uc2 (Adds comment from top \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, paragraphs 8-9)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Oct 7 (Reuters) - Japan's foreign reserves fell by a record $54 billion in September, official data showed on Friday, as global market ructions dented the value of foreign bonds and prompted dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest a steep decline in the yen.\par \par \uc2 The reserves stood at $1.238 trillion at the end of September, the lowest amount since the end of March 2017, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) data.\par \par \uc2 The data on Japan's foreign reserves, the world's second largest in size after China, came a week after separate MOF figures showed Tokyo spent up to a record 2.8 trillion yen ($19.32 billion) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market last month.\par \par \uc2 Markets have been speculating that Tokyo had sold U.S. Treasuries in conducting the dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yen's precipitous drop to 24-year lows against the greenback. Friday's MOF data appeared to back that assumption, as it showed a record drop in the value of securities, which includes U.S. Treasuries, held in reserves.\par \par \uc2 However, Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  declined to confirm if U.S. bonds were sold as part of its dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Factors behind the declines included drops in market value of securities due to big rises in bond yields, falls in the dollar value of euro-denominated assets on euro's depreciation against the dollar and selling of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Suzuki told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "I cannot comment on transactions related to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We will manage reserves by paying heed to safety and liquidity."\par \par \uc2 Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, Masato Kanda, said on Friday he had never felt there was a limit in "ammunition" available for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I've never felt any restrictions. To achieve that end, we are making various efforts," Kanda, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 FED SLIPSTREAM\par \par \uc2 Through much of this year, particularly over the past few months, the U.S. dollar has catapulted to record heights against many of its rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's aggressive policy tightening, causing a shakeout in financial markets. Surging global inflation, which is behind the Fed's action, has dented the value of bonds worldwide.\par \par \uc2 Data released this week showed foreign reserves in other Asian economies falling with South Korea posting its second-biggest monthly decline on record as authorities stepped in to counter the won's slump to a 13-1/2-year low. China and Indonesia also saw their reserves decline in September.\par \par \uc2 Japan's foreign reserves comprise cash deposits parked at overseas central banks and \uc2 Bank for International Settlements\uc2  (BIS), securities including U.S. Treasuries, gold, \uc2 IMF\uc2  reserve position and special drawing rights (SDRs).\par \par \uc2 The MOF does not reveal the makeup of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the reserves, a bulk of which is believed to be in the U.S. dollar from the past practice of dollar-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a strong yen from damaging exporters.\par \par \uc2 Yen-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been rare in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has long counted on exports of cars and electronics as a key driver of economic growth.\par \par \uc2 Now, policymakers are concerned more about the impact of sharp and one-sided yen weakening on a nascent economic recovery from the COVID-19 pandemic as it drives up living costs while making it harder for business planning.\par \par \uc2 The previous record amount for a single day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was 2.6 trillion yen spent in April 1998 during the 1997/98 Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Investors are closely watching daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data for the July-September period due out in November to see whether authorities conducted "stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  without official announcement.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not conducted dollar-selling, yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998, until the authorities forayed into the market on Sept. 22 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped sharply to a 24-year low near 146 yen to the dollar. ($1 = 144.9500 yen)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Shri Navaratnam and Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-7T10:19:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221007eia7002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
