\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Yen's pain is far from over and poised for worst year since 1970\b0\par\par\uc2 594 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2022\par 01:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 reuters://realtime/verb=Open/url=cpurl://apps.cp./Apps/\b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2 -polls?RIC=JPY= poll data\par \par \uc2 By Indradip Ghosh\par \par \uc2 BENGALURU, Oct 6 (Reuters) - Japan's yen will recoup only a third of its big losses against the dollar in the coming year as the policy gap between the ultra-hawkish \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  and the extremely dovish \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is set to widen further, a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 The policy divergence has battered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has lost over a fifth of its value this year and hit a 24-year low of 146/dollar recently, so authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since 1998 last month, spending 2.8 trillion yen.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and expectations of more to come, the yen's weakness is not over yet as \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  is unlikely to reverse his long-held pledge to keep policy ultra-loose anytime soon.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the worst performer among its G10 peers, will trade around the current 144 versus the U.S. dollar at year-end, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists in a Reuters Sept. 30-Oct. 5 poll.\par \par \uc2 If realised, the yearly loss of more than 20% would be the biggest since 1970.\par \par \uc2 "USD/JPY's uptrend unlikely to reverse as it is supported by U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy gap and balance of payment deficit, while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unilateral," said Shusuke Yamada, \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Bank of America Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  trying to manage \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume may suggest the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  not yet under pressure from the government to modify policy in response to weak yen."\par \par \uc2 This year's rise in \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields has put upward pressure on benchmark 10-year JGB yields leading the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 , which remains an outlier among global central banks, to go for massive bond-buying to protect its de facto yield cap that fuelled the yen's slide.\par \par \uc2 Core consumer inflation in Tokyo was its highest since 2014 in September and is a leading indicator of nationwide price rises. That means inflation is likely to stay above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 2% target in the near future, potentially making it harder for the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to justify its ultra-easy policy.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , which delivered its third straight 75 basis points hike last month, was expected to continue with aggressive rate hikes, paving the way for the U.S. dollar to remain strong.\par \par \uc2 Although the yen, until recently a safe haven for investors during financial market turmoil, was predicted to gain around 7% to trade at 135 against the dollar over the coming year it would be only a third of this year's losses of over 20%.\par \par \uc2 Also, nearly a third, 18 of 60 strategists predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade above the 24-year low of 145.89/$ at some point in the next year.\par \par \uc2 "The determination of the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to maintain its ultra-loose monetary stance through yield curve control has been a clear signal for selling the yen," noted \uc2 Derek Halpenny\uc2 , head of research at \uc2 MUFG\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It is hard to see a turn in USD/JPY now even after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MoF. The Fed and global central banks have more tightening to do while the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  does nothing but ease."\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the October Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll:) (Reporting by Indradip Ghosh; Polling by Prerana Bhat, Vijayalakshmi Srinivasan and Maneesh Kumar; editing by Jonathan Oatis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-10-6T00:35:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020221005eia503tvx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
