\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sterling recovers with euro as UK fiscal angst recedes, European inflation accelerates\b0\par\par\uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2022\par 07:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 30 (Reuters) - Sterling and the euro rose to fresh one-week highs on Friday, buoyed by the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 's moves to calm markets and hawkish signals from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was headed for its best week against the U.S. dollar in 2 1/2 years as the \uc2 BoE\uc2  waded into the debt market to buy gilts for a second day on Thursday, buoying UK yields.\par \par \uc2 Heated German and Dutch consumer inflation data also served as a reminder that the job of the \uc2 ECB\uc2 , \uc2 BoE\uc2  and other central banks is not done, with the figure for the wider 19-country euro zone due later on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The pound touched $1.1222 early in the Asian session, taking it very close to erasing all of the precipitous losses in the aftermath of the new government's so-called mini budget last Friday.\par \par \uc2 It gave back some of those gains later in the session but was still up 0.12% at $1.11325 at of 0522 GMT, on track for a 2.61% advance this week, the most since March 2020. That's despite plumbing a record low of $1.0327 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "The recovery in cable (the sterling-dollar rate) is very eye-catching," said Sean Callow, a strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2  in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 "It makes some sense in that UK yields are set to be high for some time, discouraging short positions. But with the UK already running very large current account deficits, we doubt there is much more upside in sterling."\par \par \uc2 The euro was about flat at $0.98145 after earlier rising as high as $0.9844.\par \par \uc2 The shared \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on track for a 1.32% weekly advance, its best showing in four months, after recovering from a fresh two-decade low at $0.9528 from Monday.\par \par \uc2 Liquidity, however, was extremely low among European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the Asian session.\par \par \uc2 Data on Thursday showed German inflation at its highest in more than a quarter of a century, driven by high energy prices, with analysts warning that the energy crisis has yet to make itself fully felt.\par \par \uc2 Inflation in the Netherlands jumped in September to its highest in decades, driven by skyrocketing energy prices, the statistics agency (\uc2 CBS\uc2 ) said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Markets are fully priced for another 75 basis point (bps) hike by the \uc2 ECB\uc2  next month, with 1-in-3 odds for a full percentage point bump.\par \par \uc2 "My choice would be 75," \uc2 ECB\uc2  policymaker Gediminas Simkus told \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  TV on the sidelines of a conference in Vilnius "But 50 is the minimum."\par \par \uc2 Colleagues including Slovakia's \uc2 Peter Kazimir\uc2 , Austria's \uc2 Robert Holzmann\uc2  and Finland's \uc2 Olli Rehn\uc2  have all put 75 bps on the table in recent days, even though the \uc2 ECB\uc2 's next meeting on Oct. 27 is still nearly a month away.\par \par \uc2 For the \uc2 BoE\uc2 , traders predict 125 bps of tightening in early November, with small odds for a 150 bps increase.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the greenback against the euro, sterling and four other major peers, managed to edge 0.12% higher to 111.93, but remained close to a one-week low of 111.64 reached overnight.\par \par \uc2 That was despite continued hawkish rhetoric from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  policymakers, with \uc2 Cleveland Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Loretta Mester\uc2  saying on Thursday that "price stability is still job one," and inflation must be tamed before officials can worry about the impact on economic growth.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was little changed at 144.55 yen, and has been mostly tracking sideways below the psychological 145 line since Japanese officials stepped in to conduct their first yen buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998 last week, when the dollar popped to a fresh 24-year peak at 145.90 yen.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  signalled on Thursday his readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves persist.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government will confirm later on Friday the amount it spent on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the amount it has left in reserve for further such action.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns are definitely out there, and putting a lid on dollar-yen," said Shinichiro Kadota, a strategist at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "But at the end of the day, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - and especially unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - don't change the direction of the market, and fundamental factors, primarily the policy divergence between the Fed and \uc2 BOJ\uc2 , will be the ultimate determinant for dollar-yen."\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the risk-sensitive Aussie slipped 0.08% to $0.6495, and New Zealand's kiwi weakened 0.1% to $0.57225, leaving both on course for their worst monthly performances since April.\par \par \uc2 That's despite market expectations for both countries' central banks to continue with rate hiking campaigns next week.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Buckland; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-30T06:54:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220930ei9u00r8l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
