\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sterling and euro recover; \uc2 ECB\uc2  likely to be aggressive after high German CPI\b0\par\par\uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2022\par 04:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 30 (Reuters) - Sterling rose to a fresh one-week high on Friday, helping to push the U.S. dollar index to a one-week low, as British policymakers moved to undo some of the damage caused by last week's tax-slashing, debt-swelling fiscal plan.               \par \par \uc2 That puts the UK \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on course for its best week in 2 1/2 years.               \par \par \uc2 The euro also jumped to a one-week peak after a heated German inflation reading reinforced expectations for more aggressive policy action from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ).               \par \par \uc2 The British pound touched $1.1222 early in the Asian session, taking it very close to erasing all of the precipitous losses in the aftermath of the new government's so-called mini budget last Friday. It was last up 0.41% at $1.11645, bringing its gain for the week to 2.87%, despite plumbing a record low of $1.0327 on Monday.               \par \par \uc2 "The recovery in cable (the sterling-dollar rate) is very eye-catching," said Sean Callow, a strategist at \uc2 Westpac\uc2  in Sydney.               \par \par \uc2 "It makes some sense in that UK yields are set to be high for some time, discouraging short positions. But with the UK already running very large current account deficits, we doubt there is much more upside in sterling."               \par \par \uc2 Overnight, sterling jumped 2.13% as the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  (\uc2 BoE\uc2 ) conducted a second day of bond buying to stabilise markets, with gilt yields also rising.               \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, British Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  and finance minister \uc2 Kwasi Kwarteng\uc2  will meet the head of the country's independent fiscal watchdog, the \uc2 Office for Budget Responsibility (OBR)\uc2 , on Friday to discuss the budget forecast process.               \par \par \uc2 Truss also vowed to stick with the controversial plans, in her first comments since the turmoil erupted in markets.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 OBR\uc2 's involvement is "alleviating fears within the markets of the so-far uncosted fiscal package, helping support GBP," said Tapas Strickland, head of market economics at \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 "A hot German CPI print also serves as a reminder of the inflation situation in Europe - and globally - and that central banks need to remain hawkish. In such a light, the \uc2 BoE\uc2 's decision on Wednesday to purchase bonds should not be read as a pivot," Strickland added.               \par \par \uc2 Data on Thursday showed German inflation at its highest in more than a quarter of a century, driven by high energy prices, with analysts warning that the energy crisis has yet to make itself fully felt.               \par \par \uc2 The reading suggests the figure for the wider 19-country euro zone, due on Friday, is also likely to exceed economists' forecasts.               \par \par \uc2 Markets are fully priced for another 75 basis point hike by the \uc2 ECB\uc2  next month, with 1-in-3 odds for a full percentage point bump.               \par \par \uc2 For the \uc2 BoE\uc2 , traders predict 125 basis points of tightening in early November, with small odds for a 150 basis-point increase.               \par \par \uc2 The euro was slightly higher on Friday at $0.9821, and earlier rose to 0.9844, the strongest level in a week.               \par \par \uc2 The shared \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains on track for a 1.29% weekly advance, its best showing in four months, after recovering from a fresh two-decade low at $0.9528 from Monday.               \par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the greenback against the euro, sterling and four other major peers, edged 0.09% higher to 111.91, but remained close to a one-week low of 111.64 reached overnight.               \par \par \uc2 That was despite continued hawkish rhetoric from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  policymakers, with \uc2 Cleveland Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Loretta Mester\uc2  saying on Thursday that "price stability is still job one," and inflation must be tamed before officials can worry about the impact on economic growth.               \par \par \uc2 The dollar appreciated 0.14% to 144.65 yen, but is mostly tracking sideways below the psychological 145 line since Japanese officials stepped in to conduct their first yen buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1998 last week, when the dollar popped to a fresh 24-year peak at 145.90 yen.               \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  signalled on Thursday his readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves persist.               \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government will confirm later on Friday the amount it spent on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the amount it has left in reserve for further such action.               \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, the dollar jumped 0.38% to 7.1247 yuan in the offshore market , putting it on track for both its best week and month since April.               \par \par \uc2 The Aussie slipped 0.08% to $0.6495, and New Zealand's kiwi weakened 0.12% to $0.5721, also leaving both on course for their worst monthly performances since April.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-30T03:25:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220930ei9u00and\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\