\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  to confirm size of yen-buying  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , eyes on size of war-chest\b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2022\par 02:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 30 (Reuters) - Japan's government will confirm on Friday the amount it spent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week to prop up the yen, which may highlight the hurdles Tokyo could face in making frequent forays into the market to stem sharp falls.\par \par \uc2 Estimates based on money market brokers showed Tokyo likely spent a record 3.6 trillion yen ($24.9 billion) on Sept. 22 in its first dollar-selling, yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 24 years to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp weakening.\par \par \uc2 A final figure will become available when the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) releases the total amount it spent for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Aug. 30 to Sept. 28, at 1000 GMT on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Japan currently holds roughly $1.3 trillion in reserves, the second biggest after China, of which $135.5 billion are held in the form of deposits parked with foreign central banks and the \uc2 Bank for International Settlements\uc2  (BIS).\par \par \uc2 The $135.5 billion in deposits can easily be tapped to finance further dollar-selling, yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This means \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is left with deposits than can finance four more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the scale conducted on Sept. 22.\par \par \uc2 "Even if it were to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely won't have to sell \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bills and instead tap this deposit for the time being," said Izuru Kato, chief economist at Totan Research, a think-tank arm of a major money market broker firm in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 If the deposits dry up, Japan would need to dip into its securities holdings sized around $1.04 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Of the main types of foreign assets Japan holds, deposits and securities are most liquid and can be converted into cash immediately.\par \par \uc2 Other forms consisted of gold, reserves at the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) reserve and \uc2 IMF\uc2  special drawing rights (SDR), though procuring dollar funds from these assets will take time, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 144.7200 yen) (Reporting by Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-30T01:09:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220930ei9u0015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
