\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sterling rallies for 3rd day after \uc2 BoE\uc2  bond buys; U.S. dollar down\b0\par\par\uc2 721 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2022\par 22:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pound rallies after 1% fall as PM defends economic plan\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 BoE\uc2  buys gilts for 2nd day\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Euro up vs dollar; German inflation soars\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  again\par \par \uc2 (Adds new analyst comment, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 29 (Reuters) - Sterling rose sharply in volatile trading on Thursday, rallying from record lows hit on Monday, after the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  conducted a second day of bond buying to stabilize financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The pound posted its largest one-day percentage gain since March 2020 and last traded at $1.1076, up 1.8%. After hitting an all-time trough of $1.0327 three days ago, sterling has rallied more than 7% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The recovery in the British \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was due in part to the \uc2 BoE\uc2 's action. On Thursday, the \uc2 BoE\uc2  bought 1.415 billion pounds ($1.55 billion) of \uc2 British government\uc2  bonds with maturities of more than 20 years, the second day of a multi-billion pound program designed to stabilize the market.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BoE\uc2  is showing creativity and willingness to respond to crazy markets," said \uc2 Greg Anderson\uc2 , global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, at \uc2 BMO Capital Markets\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 But he noted that sterling gains as a result of the \uc2 BoE\uc2 's moves are not sustainable.\par \par \uc2 "Any time a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is undertaking a temporary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  program, the market will certainly test this and see whether the central banks is going to keep doing this or not. But I wouldn't forecast that the pound's parity with the dollar is going to break."\par \par \uc2 Anderson added that he will be a seller of the pound at $1.10, with the likelihood of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  going back down to $1.05.\par \par \uc2 Sterling initially fell on Thursday as Prime Minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2  defended her government tax-cutting budget.\par \par \uc2 The dollar, on the other hand, fell against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It was last down 0.4% at 112.148.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose 0.7% against the dollar to $0.9804.\par \par \uc2 Data showed euro zone economic sentiment fell sharply and by more than expected in September as confidence dropped among companies and consumers, who are also downbeat about price trends in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 The big focus, however, was German inflation, which jumped to 10.9% this month, far beyond expectations for a reading of 10%. That suggests the figure for the wider 19-country euro zone, due on Friday, is also likely to exceed the predicted 9.6%, reinforcing the case for another 75 basis-point increase at the next \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 That said, some analysts think the \uc2 ECB\uc2 's potential action is likely just a short-term boost for the euro.\par \par \uc2 "Rate increases can support a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... But the process of inflation is never good for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially if inflation hasn't been tamed properly by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Stephen Gallo\uc2 , European head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategy at \uc2 BMO\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 "I would not want to own the euro simply because the \uc2 ECB\uc2  is hiking. I would want to own the euro when the U.S. dollar peaks, and when it becomes clear that euro zone inflation is moderating and when it becomes clear that the bloc is clear of a massive recession."\par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs, the dollar rose 0.2% to 144.355 yen .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to shore up a struggling yen. Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said on Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted to rectify market distortion caused by speculative \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. He signalled his readiness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if speculation persists.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, China's offshore yuan bounced about 1% to 7.0894 per dollar after Reuters reported state banks have been told to stock up for yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The risk-sensitive Australian dollar sank 0.4% to US$0.6494. A new measure of consumer prices showed annual inflation eased a bit from August to July, offering hope that cost pressures might be close to a peak.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss; Additional reporting by Joice Alves in London, Kevin Buckland in Tokyo, and Tom Westbrook in Singapore; Editing by Angus MacSwan, Alex Richardson, Jonathan Oatis and David Gregorio) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-29T21:08:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220929ei9t0468d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
