\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Dollar retreats, with pound rising after \uc2 BoE\uc2  announcement\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The DXY index, which measures the dollar against a basket of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell on Wednesday, 28. The dollar even advanced, but reversed, as the pound strengthened after the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  (\uc2 BoE\uc2 ) announced the purchase of long-term \uc2 British government\uc2  bonds (gilts). In addition, statements from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed) officials were on the radar, but with no news from Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In late afternoon in New York, the dollar retreated to 144.14 yen, the euro rose to $0.9733, and the pound advanced to $1.0889. The DXY index was down 1.32% at 112.604 points.\par \par \uc2 The DXY index earlier in the day renewed a 20-year high, with the euro hitting an all-time low, as the Fed's monetary tightening stance came into focus. This even after the president of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ), \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2 , said the institution will raise interest rates "in the next several meetings" in order to contain inflation in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 But the dollar lost steam throughout the day. The strengthening pound helped, after the \uc2 BoE\uc2  announced temporary buying of gilts. In the afternoon, the DXY dollar index retreated further as Oanda assessed that there was a "relief rally" in the markets following the British \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move.\par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , meanwhile, analyzed \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a report. According to the bank, Tokyo's effort may soften the dollar's advance against the yen and "buy time", but should not reverse the downward trend of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also in Asia, China today warned banks to help contain the fall of the yuan. The Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit the lowest level against the dollar since 2008 in the onshore market. Vice Chairman of the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  (\uc2 PBoC\uc2 ), \uc2 Liu Guoqiang\uc2  stressed the importance of maintaining stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and asked banks to act for stability in this market, containing fluctuations.\par \par \uc2 In the US monetary policy, the Fed's president, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , ended up not commenting on the monetary policy during a video participation in an event today, which contributed to the relief in the markets. The American \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, maintains a monetary tightening posture to contain inflation.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220929ei9s000k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
