\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Pound plunge the latest ill omen as stocks slide\b0\par\par\uc2 740 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2022\par 08:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sterling hits record low; risk of BOE response\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Euro hits 20yr low, yen sliding despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asia markets fall and S&P 500 futures drop 0.6%\par \par \uc2 By Tom Westbrook\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY, Sept 26 (Reuters) - Sterling slumped to a record low on Monday, prompting speculation of an emergency response from the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 , as confidence evaporated in Britain's plan to borrow its way out of trouble, with spooked investors piling into U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 The carnage was not confined to \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as concerns that high interest rates could hurt growth also knocked Asian shares to a two-year low, with demand-sensitive stocks such as Australia's miners and carmakers in Japan and Korea hit hard.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 futures fell 0.8% and European futures fell 0.7%. Two-year Treasury yields broke above 4.3% to a new 15-year high. The euro hit a 20-year low.\par \par \uc2 "The movements over the last couple of trading days are quite fierce," said Paul Mackel, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Hong Kong. "It's a strong reminder about how suddenly the drivers for exchange rates can change."\par \par \uc2 The pound plunged nearly 5% at one point to break beneath 1985 lows and hit $1.0327. Moves were exacerbated by thinner liquidity in the Asia session, but even after stumbling back to $1.05, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still down some 7% in just two sessions. Options pricing implies a wild ride ahead.\par \par \uc2 "The market is now treating the UK as if it's an emerging market," said \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  strategist Michael Every in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "And they're not wrong in terms of the policy response and the naivety of thinking that boosting demand rather than supply is how you deal with a supply side shock," he said.\par \par \uc2 "If this carries across into European trading you're going to get at a minimum a public statement from the BOE threatening (action) and...a strong possibility that they have to make an inter-meeting hike, and a chunky one at that."\par \par \uc2 Britain's announcement of\par \par \uc2 unfunded tax cuts\par \par \uc2 already set off the heaviest selling of gilts in three decades on Friday and has pushed the pound to a near two-year low of 92.29 pence per euro.\par \par \uc2 NOTHING IN THE DOLLAR'S WAY\par \par \uc2 The pound's plunge is only the latest unnerving move as investors' skittishness strains global financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The Nasdaq lost more than 5% last week for the second week running. The S&P 500 fell 4.8%. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to support the yen and U.S. interest rate expectations have climbed rapidly.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, MSCI's broadest index of Asia-Pacific shares outside Japan was down 1.4% to a two-year low and is heading for a monthly loss of 11%, the largest since March 2020. Japan's Nikkei fell 2.6%.\par \par \uc2 Focus later in the day will turn to politicians and policymakers' response to the plunging pound, and to the latest round of dollar strength it has unleashed.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister threatened further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, but the yen was again under pressure and fell about 0.6% to the weaker side of 144 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday announced fresh steps to slow the pace of the yuan's slide by making it sharply more expensive to bet against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though that too hardly budged the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which shot close to its daily down limit.\par \par \uc2 All that has well overshadowed Italy's election of its most right-wing government since World War Two. Some investors were relieved at the relatively poor performance of euro-sceptic coalition partners, though it was no help to the euro.\par \par \uc2 The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 20-year low of $0.9528.\par \par \uc2 Oil and gold were under pressure due to the surging greenback, with gold hitting a 2-1/2 year low of $1,626 and Brent crude futures down about 1% to the lowest since January at $85.06 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 "As of now, there doesn't seem to be anything standing in the dollar's way," said Shafali Sachdev, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fixed income and commodities for Asia at BNP Paribas Wealth Management in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Danilo Masoni in Milan; Editing by Sam Holmes and Ana Nicolaci da Costa) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-26T07:12:55.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220926ei9q00vv9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
