\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  stocks slide on  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\uc2 , weaker pound\b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2022\par 05:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Sept 26 (Reuters) - Japanese stocks kicked off the final week of the quarter on a negative note, as investors resumed trading after an extended weekend to markets that were dented by Japanese authorities' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the collapse of the British pound.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei was down 1.97% at the break on Monday after slipping as far as 26,515.06, its lowest level since July 14. The index is on course to drop for a third straight day.\par \par \uc2 The broader Topix fell 1.98%.\par \par \uc2 Stock markets tracked broader Asian peers lower as the U.S. dollar soared and bond yields strengthened amid increasing fears of a global recession. S&P 500 e-mini futures fell 0.4%.\par \par \uc2 The yen was last at 143.8 to the dollar, having weakened 2.43% since the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove it to 140.31 last week, while the benchmark 10-year Treasury yield was at 3.7185%.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since 1998 to shore up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sterling fell to an all-time low of $1.0327, extending losses from Friday after Britain's new chancellor \uc2 Kwasi Kwarteng\uc2  announced a sweeping package of tax cuts.\par \par \uc2 "There were strong expectations that the yield would settle at 3.5%, but it continued to rise and there's been selling focused on blue-chip stocks," said a domestic asset manager.\par \par \uc2 Shares of \uc2 SoftBank Group Corp\uc2  weighed on the Nikkei the most with a 4.14% drop, followed by \uc2 Tokyo Electron Ltd\uc2  and \uc2 Fast Retailing Co Ltd\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Automaker stocks also traded in red, with \uc2 Mazda Motor Corp\uc2  marking the biggest loss at 5.3% following a report that the company would stop car production in Russia.\par \par \uc2 Of the Nikkei's 225 constituents, 205 made losses, 15 advanced, and five traded flat. Every sector dropped overall.\par \par \uc2 Despite the broad losses, air and land transportation stocks traded steady as Japan prepares to re-open its borders to regular tourism next month.\par \par \uc2 "The resilience stands out, and shows increasing expectations for inbound demand due to the easing of COVID-related border restrictions," said a domestic securities broker.\par \par \uc2 Konami Group Corp\uc2  was the best performer in the Nikkei, gaining 0.89%. (Reporting by Sam Byford and Tokyo markets team; Editing by Sherry Jacob-Phillips) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-26T04:29:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220926ei9q00gtm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
