\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Speculators slash net long bets on USD -CFTC, Reuters\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2022\par 22:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds details, background, table)\par     By Saqib Iqbal Ahmed\par        NEW YORK, Sept 23 (Reuters) - Speculators' net long bets\par on the U.S. dollar fell in the latest week, according to\par calculations by Reuters and U.S. Commodity Futures Trading\par Commission data released on Friday.\par     The value of the net long dollar position was $10.23 billion\par for the week ended Sept. 20, down from a net long position of\par $17.24 billion last week.\par     U.S. dollar positioning was derived from net contracts of\par International Monetary Market speculators in the Japanese yen,\par euro, British pound, Swiss franc, and Canadian and Australian\par dollars.\par     CFTC data also showed Japanese yen net shorts increased in\par the latest week to 81,280 contracts, the largest since early\par June. Among the major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yen has struggled the most\par against the dollar as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains the only \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that is not in a tightening mode. The yen has plummeted by\par nearly 20% against the dollar this year.\par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on\par Thursday to buy yen for the first time since 1998, in an attempt\par to shore up the battered \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \par         Speculators' euro positioning, meanwhile, swung to a\par net-long position of 33,449 contracts, from a net short position\par of 11,837 contracts.\par   \par         Euro zone inflation is set to go higher and price growth\par is likely to be more persistent than earlier thought, \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Isabel Schnabel said on Thursday,\par defending the \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 's plans to raise interest rates further.\par \par   \par         CFTC data also showed speculators trimming their net\par short position on the British pound to 54,843 contracts, down\par from a net short position of 68,086 contracts.\par   \par         JAPANESE YEN (Contracts of 12,500,000 yen) \par          20 Sep 2022            Prior week\par          week             \par  Long             34,767            39,323\par  Short           116,047           120,015\par  Net             -81,280           -80,692\par  EURO (Contracts of 125,000 euros)\par          20 Sep 2022            Prior week\par          week             \par  Long            206,564           207,778\par  Short           173,115           219,615\par  Net              33,449           -11,837\par  POUND STERLING (Contracts of 62,500 pounds sterling)\par          20 Sep 2022           Prior week\par          week             \par  Long             41,289           41,129\par  Short            96,132          109,215\par  Net             -54,843          -68,086\par  SWISS FRANC (Contracts of 125,000 Swiss francs)\par          20 Sep 2022           Prior week\par          week             \par  Long              8,167            7,704\par  Short            14,907           15,009\par  Net              -6,740           -7,305\par  CANADIAN DOLLAR (Contracts of 100,000 Canadian dollars)\par          20 Sep 2022           Prior week\par          week             \par  Long             47,913           48,102\par  Short            45,857           35,677\par  Net               2,056           12,425\par  AUSTRALIAN DOLLAR (Contracts of 100,000 Aussie dollars)\par          20 Sep 2022           Prior week\par          week             \par  Long             38,797           29,218\par  Short            79,353           87,068\par  Net             -40,556          -57,850\par  MEXICAN PESO (Contracts of 500,000 pesos)\par          20 Sep 2022           Prior week\par          week             \par  Long             96,671          103,772\par  Short           124,704          129,153\par  Net             -28,033          -25,381\par  NEW ZEALAND DOLLAR (Contracts of 100,000 New Zealand dollars)\par          20 Sep 2022           Prior week\par          week             \par  Long             11,646           17,949\par  Short            24,235           23,250\par  Net             -12,589           -5,301\par  (Reporting by Saqib Iqbal Ahmed; Editing by Leslie Adler and\par David Gregorio)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-23T21:14:51.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220923ei9n03f2l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
