0.26% on Thursday, led lower by USD/JPY weakness after the BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the yen weakening near 146 in European trading, though it took back the worst of its losses. \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY fell near 5-1/2 big-figures in 1-1/2 hours amid broad dollar selling that lifted other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8226\'20\'22 During its subsequent recovery, the dollar index rose from Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s low of 110.46 to 111.21 in late U.S. trade. \u8226\'20\'22 \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed the BoJ's decision to maintain its accommodative stance. \u8226\'20\'22 Without a change in monetary policy by the BoJ, or a pivot lower by the Fed in the near-term, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not likely to have a lasting effect on USD/JPY as U.S.-Japan rates continue to diverge into 2023. \u8226\'20\'22 Though severely bruised, the 50% Fib of the 137.61-145.90 rise at 141.76 remains supportive. A close below there would put Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s low of 140.31 and 55-DMA support at 139.86 in focus. \u8226\'20\'22 Sterling suffered tumult of its own, though it was ending NorAm -0.03% at 1.1266. \u8226\'20\'22 The pound had rallied to 1.1365 ahead of the \uc2 BoE\uc2  rate announcement. Traders' hopes for a 75bp hike, which would keep pace with Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s Fed hike, were dashed when the \uc2 BoE\uc2  hiked by 50bp, pushing the pound to lows by 1.1242. \u8226\'20\'22 The \uc2 BoE\uc2  vote was 5-4 with 3 dissenters voting for +75bp, while new MPC member Swati Dhingra voted for +25bp. \u8226\'20\'22 Sterling traders' attention now turns to Friday\u8217\'20\'19s fiscal statement from finance minister Kwasi Kwarteng for hints at the degree of stimulus Prime Minister Liz Truss is willing to provide to arrest the effects of high inflation and recession. \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD is ending NorAm near flat at 0.9840, trading in a relatively slight 1 big-figure range. \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY\u8217\'20\'19s recovery above 140 bodes well for further EUR gains. On the margins, the \uc2 BoJ\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as yet to be backed up by higher rates, may signal developed market central banks may be willing to act to stall the dollar's rise. \u8226\'20\'22 Rising global rates may stir EUR/USD buying off current lows. \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Isabel Schnabel said that inflation may be more persistent than thought, which may hint at a more hawkish stance to come. EURIBOR rates were also moving higher, the peak in \uc2 ECB\uc2  rates now at 3.13% in September 2023. \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields moved higher with the 2-year note ending NorAm at 4.12%, the 10-yr at 3.69%. The key 2-10 spread was at -42bp up from -57.8bp overnight. \u8226\'20\'22 Cryptocurrencies shrugged off higher rates, with bitcoin up 3% at $19k, while ETH up 3% at $1,283. \u8226\'20\'22 Equities continued their move lower, with the S&P 500 down 0.82% at 3,761, eyeing support at the June 15 low at 3,721 and the June 17 low at 3,637. Commentary and Analysis EUR/USD-After \uc2 BOJ\uc2  some hope emerges for longs \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD rallied from 0.9807 to 0.9908 after \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken yen \u8226\'20\'22 NY opened near 0.9880, pair slide in early trade as US$ buyers emerged \u8226\'20\'22 0.9811 hit on EBS, dip was bout & pair neared 0.9850 late in the day \u8226\'20\'22 Lift aided by US rates giving up some earlier gains \u8226\'20\'22 US$ sales & EUR/JPY rally above 140.00 also help underpin EUR/USD \u8226\'20\'22 Pair traded up near +0.10% on the session which lead to warnings for shorts \u8226\'20\'22 Daily doji candle formed & daily RSI diverged; imply short squeeze risk \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows how much help EUR/USD needs to rally USD/JPY rally derailed by BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , for now \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY ending tumultuous day -1.34% at 142.19; Thurs range 145.90-140.31 \u8226\'20\'22 Overnight gain to 145.90 reversed as BoJ makes good on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threat \u8226\'20\'22 Pair slid to 140.31 in Europe, higher into NorAm, NY range 142.53-140.35 \u8226\'20\'22 \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , BoJ accommodation spark dollar whipsaw vs yen \u8226\'20\'22 Key 50% Fib of 137.61-145.90 rise bruised but intact on closing basis \u8226\'20\'22 Close below opens way for test of Thurs low 140.31, 55-DMA at 139.86 \u8226\'20\'22 Res 142.39 NorAm afternoon pullback high from NY low, 142.81 early NY high \u8226\'20\'22 Barring further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or BoJ pivot to higher rates USD likely to retest 2022 highs \uc2 BoE\uc2 's dovish 50bp hike disappointment sends GBP careening toward 2022 lows \u8226\'20\'22 GBP/USD soft into NY close -0.1% at 1.1256; NorAm range 1.1347-1.1242 \u8226\'20\'22 Pair had rallied to 1.1365 just ahead of \uc2 BoE\uc2  +50bp rate announcement \u8226\'20\'22 Disappointed traders hoped for +75 from \uc2 BoE\uc2  sold GBP hard \u8226\'20\'22 Sterling bulls gutted after 50bp \uc2 BoE\uc2  hike falls behind Fed \u8226\'20\'22 Fri's fiscal stmt by FinMin Kwarteng, 9.30AM GMT; tax cuts, energy subsidy \u8226\'20\'22 Support at 1.1213 Thurs 2022 low, 1.1193 lower 30-d Bolli in focus \u8226\'20\'22 Res 1.1294 10-HMA, 1.1365 Thurs pre-BoE high, 1.1535 21-DMA \u8226\'20\'22 Tepid BoE hike path, fiscal accommodation keeps risks tilted to downside \u8226\'20\'22 March 1985 lows by 1.1060, 1.0805 and 1.0520 likely come into sharper focus AUD/USD-Bull fight to maintain post-\uc2 BOJ\uc2  gains \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD rallied from 0.6574 after the \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the yen \u8226\'20\'22 0.6669 traded, NY opened near 0.6645, pair then rallied to 0.6670 \u8226\'20\'22 US$ buying emerged however, 0.6615 neared but the fall halted \u8226\'20\'22 US$ buying abated & USD/CNH weakened, 0.6650 neared late, pair +0.23% \u8226\'20\'22 US rates slip from highs, equity bounce help buoy AUD/USD \u8226\'20\'22 Daily RSI diverged on new low; long legged doji formed; warnings for bears \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  blip shows how much help EUR/USD needs to rally EUR/USD rose on Thursday but only after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered a wave of dollar sales, demonstrating the scale of assistance it would take to spark a significant euro rally. Before the \uc2 BOJ\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , EUR/USD hit a fresh 20-year low as investors priced in a higher terminal U.S. rates after the Fed delivered hawkish projections on Thursday. EUR/USD rallied as high as 0.9908 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the gains were already eroding in early U.S. trade. The dollar still holds a significant yield advantage over the euro even after protracted tightening in German-U.S. 2-year spreads, which has not been enough to reverse EUR/USD's down trend. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  would have to become much more aggressive with rate hikes than currently expected to significantly diminish the U.S. yield advantage, but there are reasons to doubt it will. The potential for escalation of the Ukraine war could keep energy prices elevated this winter, leading analysts to expect a harsher recession. \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  expects euro zone GDP to fall near 3.0% by mid-2023, which could temper the \uc2 ECB\uc2 's hiking enthusiasm and prevent EUR/USD from mounting significant rallies. Charts: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3xJz523"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 & {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3qYQAHW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  Sterling bulls gutted after 50bp \uc2 BoE\uc2  hike falls behind Fed GBP/USD fell on Thursday and appeared headed toward a test of the 37-year low of 1.1213 it struck before Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened the dollar, as markets expressed disappointment with \uc2 BoE\uc2 's paltry half-point hike, which could leave a slew of support vulnerable. Futures markets had been pricing in a 75bp hike, and the 50bp move leaves the UK lagging the pace set by the Fed's three-quarter-point increase on Wednesday, and is unlikely to halt UK inflation, which the \uc2 BoE\uc2  expects to be 11% in October even after lowering its forecast. While the \uc2 BoE\uc2  has vowed to "respond forcefully, as necessary" to rising prices, fiscal measures by the new prime minister to be released Friday are expected to include price controls on energy and tax cuts that could ultimately prevent inflation from falling while adding to the ominous current account deficit. The \uc2 BoE\uc2  hike disappointment put support at Thursday's 2022 low 1.1213 back in focus, with further tests of support at the lower 30-day Bolli at 1.1194 and March 1985 weekly lows of 1.1060 and 1.0805 likely. Chart: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3Uz8wGD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  Chart of the Day (USD/JPY) USD/JPY fell on Thursday but recovered 1.1% off its early U.S. low of 140.35 as bids emerged above 140 after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , suggesting a range between there and a potential BoJ-enforced top by 146 could develop. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after USD/JPY climbed near 146 following the BoJ's decision to keep rates steady at -0.1% and dovish comments by Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2 . Though it made good on prior threats about disorderly market moves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may turn out to be a stop-gap measure with the BoJ sticking to its accommodative monetary policy stance while other developed and emerging market central banks lift rates to stem rising inflation. Traders appear to be seeking to reestablish longs near 140 and are likely to continue testing the \uc2 BoJ\uc2 's resolve. USD/JPY finds support at Thursday's NorAm pullback low of 140.74, the post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight low of 140.31 and the big-figure and option interest area around 140. Without continued BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or a change in its rate policy, USD/JPY remains likely to re-test 24-year highs above 146 on the way to 150. Chart: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3R5OUXU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-25T19:10:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220922ei9m03nbt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
