\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : DXY Dollar Index Advances; EUR and Pound Bearish\b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The DXY index, which measures the dollar against a basket of strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose on Thursday, 22, still on the heels of the previous day's interest rate hike by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 . In addition, other major central banks announced decisions, with several of them tightening monetary policy to contain interest rates. In Europe, the euro and the pound retreated, the latter even as the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  (\uc2 BoE\uc2 ) raised interest rates this morning. The Yen was in focus and rose after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government announced its first \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 24 years.\par \par \uc2 By late afternoon in New York the dollar was down at 142.34 Yen, the euro was down at $0.9846, and the pound was down at $1.1264. The DXY index registered a 0.64% rise, at 111.353 points.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's stance of maintaining interest rate hikes, signaling that more is to come, continued to support the dollar today. The euro, on the other hand, retreated. On the European indicator agenda, the euro zone's consumer confidence index fell to -28.8 in September, at an all-time low and below the -25.6 forecast of analysts heard by the Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 In Asia, the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ) maintained monetary policy as expected. The local government, however, announced that it will buy yen, in the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its kind in more than two decades in the country. Some analysts questioned whether the yen will remain at a contained level for long, with \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  also highlighting potential challenges ahead in this strategy.\par \par \uc2 The pound fluctuated against the dollar after the \uc2 BoE\uc2  raised interest rates by 50 basis points in a split decision. Several agents, such as ING, predicted more hikes by the \uc2 BoE\uc2  later this year. In Switzerland, the local BC said goodbye to negative interest rates, when it raised its basic rate by 75 basis points, to 0.50%, in line with market expectations. At the time quoted the dollar was up at 0.9769 Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 Among other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in focus, the dollar was down at 17.5987 rand after \uc2 South Africa's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised its key interest rate by 75 basis points to 6.25%, also in the face of high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220923ei9m00464\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
