\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The super dollar does not stop the escalation after the Fed meeting and its impact on emerging markets is a concern\b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar reaches a 20-year high on Thursday, one day after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's interest rate hike. However, it falls against the yen, after the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, and against the British pound after its rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Today's dollar and today's blue dollar: up-to-the-minute quotes on Thursday, September 22nd. The US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched multi-year highs in early trading, a day after the Fed raised its rate to a range of 3%-3.25%. The dollar index, which compares the greenback to a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rose to 111.81 for the first time since mid-2002, later settling at 110.940.\par \par \uc2 The yen strengthened sharply on Thursday after Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since 1998 to shore up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar fell as low as 140.31 yen and later retreated 1.2 percent to 142.37 yen in a day of volatile trading. The euro, the Australian dollar and the pound sterling also fell against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Follow the price of the blue, official, CCL and MEP dollar in Argentina. It was \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the yen since 1998 and came in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to maintain ultra-low interest rates, which sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling. "What Japan is doing is sending a signal that pushing dollar/yen higher is not a free ride," said \uc2 Jane Foley\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  speaking to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 However, she added: "Given that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  has just implemented a very loose monetary policy, just after the Fed has adopted a more hawkish stance, I think the fundamentals will push dollar/yen higher."\par \par \uc2 The euro weakened against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , touching a new 20-year low of $0.9807, and sterling fell to a new 37-year low of $1.1213, although it is recovering to $1.1250 following the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2 's announcement to raise interest rates by 50 basis points.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220922ei9m007t5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
