\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen as Unlikely to Support the Yen for Long -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 145 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par 14:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0855 ET - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to change the yen's weakening trend, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's \uc2 George Saravelos\uc2  says in a report. "It is simply not credible for a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be debasing its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via extreme amounts of QE while authorities pursue a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the same time," Saravelos says. "For the JPY to start strengthening either the global dollar positive environment needs to turn or the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  needs to abandon" it's cap on yields. Saravelos worries that "\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will just lead to an unnecessary loss of reserves and credibility." The yen rises 2.5% versus the dollar, which is also weakening against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 22, 2022 08:55 ET (12:55 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220922ei9m001r9\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 RTTN\par \b \uc2 Japanese Yen Gains Ground Following BoJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 editorial@rttnews.com (RTT Staff Writer) \par \uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par \uc2 RTT News\par \uc2 RTTNEW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022 RTTNews. All rights reserved \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen appreciated against its major counterparts in the European session on Thursday, after the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide amid the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ultra-loose policy.\par \par \uc2 Shortly after the \uc2 BoJ\uc2 's decision to maintain ultra-low interest rates, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time since 1998.\par \par \uc2 The move was aimed to shore up the value of the yen due to the interest rate gap between the United States and Japan.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the \uc2 BoJ\uc2  decided to maintain a negative interest rate of -0.1 percent on current accounts that financial institutions maintain at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank will continue to purchase a necessary amount of Japanese government bonds without setting an upper limit so that 10-year JGB yields will remain at around zero percent.\par \par \uc2 This was followed by a third straight 75 basis point rate hike from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  on Wednesday, which sent the yen plunging a 24-year low against the U.S. dollar in the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The yen climbed to more than 2-week highs of 140.65 against the greenback and 139.25 against the euro, from an early 24-year low of 145.90 and a 2-day low of 143.70, respectively. The yen is likely to challenge resistance around 138.00 against the greenback and 136.00 against the euro.\par \par \uc2 The yen rallied to a 1-1/2-month high of 82.80 against the kiwi, multi-week highs of 104.83 against the loonie and 93.81 against the aussie, up from its previous 2-day lows of 85.06, 108.15 and 96.41, respectively. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may face resistance around 80.00 against the kiwi, 102.00 against the loonie and 92.00 against the aussie.\par \par \uc2 The yen advanced to a 1-1/2-month high of 159.59 against the pound and more than a 2-week high of 144.34 against the franc, following an early 2-day low of 164.43 and a multi-year low of 151.47, respectively. The next possible resistance for the yen is seen around 157.00 against the pound and 142.00 against the franc.\par \par \uc2 Looking ahead, Canada new housing price index for August, U.S. weekly jobless claims for the week ended September 17 and leading index for August will be featured in the New York session.\par \par \uc2 At 10:00 am ET, Eurozone flash consumer sentiment index for September is due.\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTTNEW0020220922ei9m001s0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
