\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW- \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen\b0\par\par\uc2 1,162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices)\par \par \uc2 LONDON/TOKYO, Sept 22(Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday for the first time since 1998 to shore up the battered yen, in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to maintain ultra-low interest rates that have hammered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We have taken decisive action (in the exchange market)," vice finance minister for international affairs Masato Kanda told reporters, responding in the affirmative when asked if that meant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen jumped by as much as 2.2% against the U.S. dollar to around 140.31 yen after the announcement. The Bank of Japan's commitment to super-low interest rates had weighed on the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has lost 22% in value this year.\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 24-year low of 145.90 against the dollar. It was last up 0.8% on the day against the dollar at 142.90 and up 0.5% against the euro at 140.99.\par \par \uc2 COMMENTS:\par \par \uc2 JOE LIN, DIRECTOR OF INVESTMENTS, GOLDEN EQUATOR WEALTH, SINGAPORE\par \par \uc2 "This sort of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not be able to overpower the discrepancy in monetary policy between the U.S. and Japan \u8230\'20\'26 Where you can really move the needle, comes when you have an increment in interest rates."\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow you\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a knee-jerk reaction and yen will strengthen a little bit, but after a while, it\u8217\'20\'19s just going to move back to the 145 level.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the near term, (there is) almost no scenario that you can see a reversal in this trend. It\u8217\'20\'19s just whether they can keep it sort of controlled or within a rangebound dynamic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 NAKA MATSUZAWA, CHIEF JAPAN MACRO STRATEGIST, \uc2 NOMURA\uc2 , TOKYO:\par \par \uc2 "There are two things from here: One, how the U.S. counterpart responds, and two, what (Prime Minister Fumio)Kishida says about it.\par \par \uc2 "I think it's hard for Japan now to get a welcoming message from the U.S. on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is not changing their easing bias, and the U.S. wants the dollar to be strong to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Without moving away from Abenomics, the policy doesn't change from weakening the yen, (and the effect may be shortlived).\par \par \uc2 "In short, I think this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is probably done by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone, without the backing of the U.S. and perhaps without the backing of the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 . Only when Kishida appoints a new governor to the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  that's when a strong message can be sent to the market."\par \par \uc2 TORU SUEHIRO, CHIEF ECONOMIST, \uc2 DAIWA SECURITIES\uc2 , TOKYO\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith the Tokyo market closed tomorrow (on a national holiday) and the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to maintain policy today, there was an increasing risk of the yen sliding further in a thin market. The government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the very last minute this evening after the rate hit the line that prompted the rate checks last week and before the market can get volatile.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe line of 145-146 yen per dollar will be seen as the ceiling for a while. But the next FOMC is looming in just over a month and the U.S. Fed keeps up with rate hikes, much remains uncertain about the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s course depending on indicators coming till then. If the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s rate hike is seen accelerating, the risk of further yen weakening is of course remaining.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must check the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response \u8211\'20\'13 if they issue comments that signal some level of understanding on the yen\u8217\'20\'19s rapid weakening and the Japanese government\u8217\'20\'19s action, then the risk of further yen decline will be smaller. Otherwise, Japan wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to take the step again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 BEN LAIDLER, GLOBAL MARKETS STRATEGIST, \uc2 ETORO\uc2 , LONDON:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe first Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in near a quarter century is a significant, but ultimately doomed step to defend the yen. It has been the dramatic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  outlier this year, losing over 20% of its value versus the dollar. But this has been fundamentally driven, with Japanese interest rates rock-bottom and economic growth sluggish. As long as the Fed stays on the hawkish, rate-raising front foot, any yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to only slow, not halt, the yen slide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DEREK HALPENNY\uc2 , HEAD OF GLOBAL MARKETS RESEARCH, \uc2 MUFG\uc2 , LONDON:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnless there is a clear shift in the fundamental backdrop driving Japanese yen weaker, the ability to turn the trend is limited.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may see this as buying some time and hope that the Fed completes its tightening cycle by year-end. which may help to bring some degree of turn in the trend.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 JANE FOLEY\uc2 , HEAD OF \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGY, RABOBANK, LONDON\par \par \uc2 "If this move was aimed at slowing the upside in dollar/yen it could have an impact. Will it be successful in turning dollar/yen around? I don't think so.\par \par \uc2 "Given that we just had the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  underpinning a very loose monetary policy and that came just after the Fed underpinned a hawkish outlook, I think the fundamentals will drive dollar/yen higher.\par \par \uc2 "But what Japan is doing is sending a signal that it's not a free ride to drive dollar/yen higher."\par \par \uc2 TAKESHI MINAMI, CHIEF ECONOMIST AT NORINCHUKIN RESEARCH INSTITUTE, TOKYO\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith rate hikes by the Fed and \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2 , that widened the interest rate gap between Japan and overseas, Japan took the actual step further than a verbal warning. Because the market was expecting no actual action, the government apparently tried to change the view.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 SIMON HARVEY\uc2 , HEAD OF \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  ANALYSIS, MONEX, LONDON\par \par \uc2 "For traders, the lip service from Japanese officials this year was always viewed as a short-term hurdle, as they have repeatedly shown a lack of appetite to follow it up with actual \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This has now changed, with the BoJ taking the fight to the yen shorts.\par \par \uc2 While this policy will be successful in driving dollar-yen lower in the short-term, policymakers' ability to take dollar-yen lower over the medium-term is subject to more scepticism under the Fed's aggressively hawkish stance and the limited nature of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 In order to achieve a stronger yen over the medium-term, we continue to believe that the \uc2 BoJ\uc2  will need to abandon its ultra-loose policy stance as \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts will prove unsustainable."\par \par \uc2 KAMAL SHARMA, SENIOR \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, \uc2 BANK OF AMERICA\uc2 , LONDON\par \par \uc2 "The next logical step was to actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , now it seems from the headlines that this is unilateral, as opposed to multilateral, so it\u8217\'20\'19s just the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance interveneing\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than the Japanese asking for the assistance of other central banks. Ultimately, the question will be: how much has it been?"\par \par \uc2 "For the time being, that has injected some more two-way risk into dollar-yen."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tokyo bureau, London Markets Team; editing by Amanda Cooper) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-22T11:26:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220922ei9m01s77\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
