\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes \highlight\uc2  in the  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\uc2  market to halt yen's decline\b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sep 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday for the first time since 1998 to prop up the battered yen after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to maintain ultra-low interest rates sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling.\par \par \uc2 "We have taken decisive action (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market)," Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Masato Kanda told reporters, answering in the affirmative when asked if that meant \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The move came hours after the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep interest rates at extraordinarily low levels to support economic growth, running counter to a global wave of monetary tightening by central banks struggling to curb rising inflation.\par \par \uc2 "There is no change in our stance of maintaining loose monetary policy for the time being. We will not raise interest rates for some time," \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  said at a briefing following the decision.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's decision came after the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  on Wednesday made its third consecutive interest rate hike of 75 basis points and signaled more hikes, underscoring its resolve not to let up in its fight against inflation.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was down nearly 1 percent to 143.5 yen after trading more than 1 percent higher against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara; additional reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto, Kantaro Komiya, Daniel Leussink, Kaori Kaneko and Takaya Yamaguchi; editing by Richard Pullin, Sam Holmes and Kim Coghill, translated by Tom\u225\'00\'E1s Cobos)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220922ei9m004uw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
