\par\par \b \uc2 Interest-Rate Hikes Come Thick and Fast on 'Super Thursday' -- WSJ\b0\par\par\uc2 By Quentin Webb \par \uc2 403 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2022\par 11:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Following Wednesday's interest-rate raise by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , a string of other central banks are adjusting monetary policy, on what ING dubs "Super Thursday." ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://think.ing.com/articles/rates-spark-super-thursday"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://think.ing.com/articles/rates-spark-super-thursday}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Here's what has happened so far: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- Japan: An outlier, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  kept its benchmark rate at minus \par       0.1%] \par       (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bank-of-japan-maintains-ultralow-interest-rates-11663815848"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/bank-of-\b  \highlight22japan\b0 \highlight22 -maintains-ultralow-interest-rates-11663815848}}}\uc2 \f2 ). \par       Tokyo later \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to [shore up the yen. \par       (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-news-today-09-22-2022/card/yen-rallies-after-tokyo-intervenes-to-support-currency-kecKl56FgD2DB20AfLi4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-news-today-09-22-2022/card/yen-rallies-after-tokyo-\b  \highlight22intervenes\b0 \highlight22 -to-support-\b  \highlight22currency\b0 \highlight22 -kecKl56FgD2DB20AfLi4}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \par  \par  \par    -- Switzerland: Raised rates by 0.75 point to 0.5% \par       (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/swiss-national-bank-raises-interest-rates-by-75-basis-points-11663832982"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/swiss-national-bank-raises-interest-rates-by-75-basis-points-11663832982}}}\uc2 \f2 ), \par       making it one of the last central banks to exit negative territory. \par  \par    -- Norway: Increased rates by 0.5 point to 2.25%. \par  \par    -- Indonesia: Raised its benchmark rate by 0.5 percentage poin \par       (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/indonesias-central-bank-raises-rates-again-to-tamp-down-inflation-11663834184)t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/indonesias-\b  \highlight22central-bank\b0 \highlight22 -raises-rates-again-to-tamp-down-inflation-11663834184)t}}}\uc2 \f2  \par       to 4.25%. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And here's what markets are waiting for: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -- U.K.: The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision, postponed after the death of Queen \par       Elizabeth II \par       (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-news-today-09-09-2022/card/hold-bank-of-england-coDXwFzkIKPQvVulj3Cw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-news-today-09-09-2022/card/hold-bank-of-england-coDXwFzkIKPQvVulj3Cw}}}\uc2 \f2 ), \par       is due at 7 a.m. ET. \par  \par    -- Turkey: After cutting interest rates \par       (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/turkeys-central-bank-cuts-rates-in-surprise-decision-11660826963"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/turkeys-\b  \highlight22central-bank\b0 \highlight22 -cuts-rates-in-surprise-decision-11660826963}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \par       in August, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Turkey's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is meeting again. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  recently said](\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/09/15/risk-of-global-recession-in-2023-rises-amid-simultaneous-rate-hikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/09/15/risk-of-global-recession-in-2023-rises-amid-simultaneous-rate-hikes}}}\uc2 \f2 ) global central banks were "raising interest rates this year with a degree of synchronicity not seen over the past five decades" and [warned tighter policy could spark a global recession next year (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/world-bank-warns-of-global-recession-next-year-if-central-banks-lift-interest-rates-too-high-11663259402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.wsj.com/articles/world-bank-warns-of-global-recession-next-year-if-central-banks-lift-interest-rates-too-high-11663259402}}}\uc2 \f2 ).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NOTE: In-line links reference additional content of interest chosen by the WSJ news team.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This item is part of a Wall Street Journal live coverage event. The full stream can be found by searching P/WSJL (WSJ Live Coverage).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 22, 2022 05:15 ET (09:15 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220922ei9m000tf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
