\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Asia\u8217\'20\'19s macro hedge funds get ready for end of yen weakness\b0\par\par\uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2022\par 11:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds full name of fund management company in paragraph 4)\par \par \uc2 By Summer Zhen\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Asia macro hedge fund managers, many of whom posted strong returns this year, are betting the Japanese yen's unrelenting slide will end soon and some are even priming for a possible tumble in Japanese government bonds.\par \par \uc2 Veteran Japan investor Soon Hock Chua's Asia Genesis Macro Fund closed its short position on yen recently after the short trade contributed about 3 percentage points of the gross return this year. The Singapore-based fund had a net return of 9.3% at the end of August.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had short positions in yen since January and closed them at slightly above the 140 level. We are neutral at the current level,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chua, the fund's chief investment officer.\par \par \uc2 Chua founded Asia Genesis Asset Management in 1999 and his Japan Macro Fund returned 18.7% annually between March 2000 and 2009. He relaunched the business in 2020 after taking a break.\par \par \uc2 "Japanese authorities rightly should be concerned about the very weak yen and may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Chua said, pointing to the jump in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation.\par \par \uc2 The growing divergence between the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's ultra-dovish policy and the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's super-hawkish one has driven the yen down 20% this year against the dollar. The Fed is widely expected to deliver another aggressive hike later on Wednesday, with the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  seen standing pat again on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's zero-rates policy stance, even as Japan's inflation has hit its fastest annual pace in nearly eight years, has speculators betting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will eventually have to give up on the vast bond buying project that keeps 10-year yields pinned to zero.\par \par \uc2 "A change of monetary policy is long overdue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shun Hong Liu, chief investment officer of Hong Kong-based Hong Investment Advisors. Its HCM Rapier Fund Class A generated a 55% net return through the end of August 2022.\par \par \uc2 Bucking the trend of many other funds, Liu has a long position on the yen at 130-per-dollar and believes a sharp appreciation of the yen could easily happen, like it did in 1998 and 2008.\par \par \uc2 It would not be a surprise if the Japanese politicians ask \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  to discontinue the ceiling of 0.25% on 10-year JGBs and try to steer the economy away from trouble before his retirement, Liu said. Kuroda retires next year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have conviction in our long yen position,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that the positions so far haven\u8217\'20\'19t affected performance too much as they use the long positions as a hedge on their other short Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades.\par \par \uc2 Chua and Liu also warn that JGBs are a bubble that may burst soon, as Japan's monetary stimulus had merely stoked inflation, instead of generating sustainable economic growth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJapan will see the bursting of JGB bubble that it desperately wants to preserve,\u8221\'20\'1D Chua said. "If the yen weakens further and CPI inflation escalates above 3% for a sustained period, this may be coming."\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, betting against Japanese sovereign debt-- a trade famously known as a widow-maker -- has never been easy, given the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's massive balance sheet and steely resolve to defend its yield curve control settings.\par \par \uc2 Asia Genesis Macro Fund\u8217\'20\'19s short trades on JGBs were closed out with a 1.2% gross loss this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \u8217\'20\'19widow\u8217\'20\'19 trade remains challenging as Kuroda's \uc2 BOJ\uc2  remains steadfast,\u8221\'20\'1D Chua said. (Reporting by Summer Zhen Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-21T10:58:03.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220921ei9l01mke\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
