\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Super dollar nears two-decade highs ahead of Fed rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose and held near two-decade highs against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, biding its time ahead of a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings including one by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  that will likely decide on another sharp rate hike.\par \par \uc2 Follow the price of the blue, official, CCL and MEP dollar in Argentina. Trading was generally subdued, with London and Tokyo markets closed for public holidays.\par \par \uc2 Today's dollar and today's blue dollar: up-to-the-minute quotes on Monday, September 19 Global stock markets remained jittery and the dollar maintained its firm tone, given expectations that the Fed would maintain its aggressive rate hike path to contain uncomfortably high inflation.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which measures the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against six peers, rose 0.164% to trade near the 20-year high of 110.79 reached on September 7.\par \par \uc2 As last week's data showed a broad-based rise in underlying U.S. consumer prices, markets have contemplated the possibility of a 100 basis point rate hike when the Fed concludes its two-day meeting on Wednesday. Markets are fully discounting a 75bp hike and about a 20% chance of 100bp.\par \par \uc2 This week is also dotted with holidays that could reduce liquidity and lead to more pronounced price movements, with markets in Japan and the UK closed on Monday, Australia on Thursday and Japan again on Friday, among others.\par \par \uc2 The euro was down 0.05% at $1.001. The dollar strengthened about 0.24% to 144.99 yen, floating just below a strong resistance level at 145 that has been bolstered by hawkish comments from Japanese monetary authorities about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would maintain its massive stimulus at its meeting on Wednesday and Thursday, continuing its ultra-expansionary monetary policy. But, a turning point may come sooner than expected, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently dropped the word "temporary" for its description of elevated inflation.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220919ei9j006v3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
