\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar advances as markets brace for hefty Fed rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 974 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2022\par 16:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Markets in consolidation mode ahead of Fed policy decision\par     * Fed funds futures price in 21% chance of 100-basis-point hike\par     * China's yuan hits new 26-month low against dollar\par     * New Zealand dollar falls to lowest level since May 2020\par \par  (Adds new analyst comment, byline, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  table, updates prices)\par     By Dhara Ranasinghe and Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par     LONDON/NEW YORK, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The dollar gained against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday, trading\par within narrow ranges ahead of a slew of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meetings this week led by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which is\par likely to deliver another hefty interest rate hike.\par     Trade was generally subdued, with markets in London and Tokyo closed for public holidays.\par     World stock markets remained on edge and the dollar maintained its firm tone, given expectations that\par the Fed would maintain its aggressive tightening path to contain uncomfortably high inflation.\par     "On a high level, the greenback is benefiting from a continued sell-off in global equities," said John\par Doyle, vice president of trading and dealing at Monex USA in Washington.\par     "With the Fed's decision pending, I think the dollar will continue to take its cues from overall risk\par sentiment. We do not think the Fed will hike 100 basis points this week, but the potential is still real,"\par he added.\par     Fed funds futures have priced in a 79% chance of a 75-basis-point rate hike this week and a 21%\par probability of a 100-basis-point increase at the conclusion of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's two-day policy\par meeting, according to Refinitiv data.\par     The dollar index, which measures the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against six counterparts, was up 0.4% at 109.98,\par not far from 20-year high of 110.79 hit on Sept. 7.    \par     This week is also smattered with holidays that could thin liquidity and result in sharper price moves,\par with Japan and Britain off on Monday, Australia on Thursday, and Japan again on Friday, among others.\par     In other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the euro was 0.3% lower against the dollar at $0.9984, sterling was 0.4%\par weaker at $1.1386 and within sight of Friday's 37-year lows, while the New Zealand and Australian\par dollars fell 0.8% and 0.5%, respectively.\par     The New Zealand dollar fell to its lowest level since May 2020 of US$0.5933, and was last at US$0.5937\par .\par     The Canadian dollar fell to its lowest level in almost two years at C$1.3324 per U.S. dollar.\par     "The drop in oil has allowed a modest rally against commodity-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the Canadian\par dollar," said Monex's Doyle.\par     The dollar was around 0.4% firmer at 143.50 yen, hovering beneath a strong resistance level at\par 145 that has been reinforced by Japanese policymakers' toughened talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is widely expected to stick with massive stimulus at its meeting on Wednesday and\par Thursday, keeping its ultra-loose policy in place. But a turning point in Japanese monetary policy may come\par sooner than has been thought, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently dropping the word "temporary" for its\par description of elevated inflation.\par     China's yuan ended at a fresh 26-month low on Monday and traded below the psychologically critical\par 7-per-dollar level. In offshore trade, the yuan was 0.35 weaker.\par     Bitcoin, the biggest cryptocurrency by market value, fell to a three-month low below $19,000,\par as unease over rising interest rates globally knocked risk assets. It was last down 0.9% at\par $19,241.\par     Ether, the cryptocurrency used in the Ethereum blockchain, rallied from a two-month low against the\par dollar and was last up 1.8% on the day at $1,358. \par     Ethereum went through a major software upgrade last week that alters the way ether tokens are created,\par drastically reducing its energy usage.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:34AM (1434 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 109.8700       109.5500    +0.31%         14.851%       +110.1800   +109.4800\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9995        $1.0015     -0.20%         -12.08%       +$1.0029    +$0.9966\par  Dollar/Yen                   143.4100       142.9400    +0.33%         +24.57%       +143.6400   +142.6500\par  Euro/Yen                     143.35         143.13      +0.15%         +10.00%       +143.5400   +142.8100\par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.9666         0.9644      +0.26%         +6.01%        +0.9695     +0.9630\par  Sterling/Dollar              $1.1398        $1.1422     -0.21%         -15.72%       +$1.1441    +$1.1