\par\par \b \uc2 Divergent Fed, BoJ Paths to Determine  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Trend -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2022\par 15:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0926 ET - The dollar's strength versus the yen will likely be determined by divergent monetary policy, \uc2 Barclays\uc2  ' Shinichiro Kadota and Lhamsuren Sharavdemberel say in a report. "Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  [in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] has escalated with the pair approaching its YTD high of 145," they write. The US is unlikely to participate in a joint USD-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and "any unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could...fail to mark a turn in the long-term trend," they say. The Fed is expected to hike by 75 basis points next week and the \uc2 BoJ\uc2  is seen as keeping rates below zero. The USD rises against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  today, except the yen, which is at 143.22 per dollar. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0911 ET - Sterling may extend its losses as U.K. real interest rates adjusted for inflation could move further into negative territory even if the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  tightens policy further at its next meeting, Unicredit Research says. "The U.K. economy is sluggish--retail sales plunged in August--while inflation remains high and further tightening by the BOE--we expect a 50 basis points interest rate hike to 2.25% on Thursday--is unlikely to be enough to compensate for it," \uc2 Unicredit\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Roberto Mialich says in a note. Real rates could therefore become more negative, weakening sterling against the dollar and the euro towards 1.10 and 0.90, respectively, he says. GBP/USD falls 0.8% to 1.1380 and EUR/GBP rises 0.4% to 0.8751. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0855 ET - The two-year yield rises while the 10-year wobbles, widening a curve inversion often seen as a sign investors are bracing for recession. Pundits have all but ruled out a dovish 50-basis point rate increase next week, with 100bp becoming the alternative to a more likely 75bp hike. "The widening of the spread between the 2 and 10 TSY clearly indicates a full-blown recession by year end," \uc2 Spartan\uc2  's Peter Cardillo says in a note. The overall concern is that monetary tightening would lead to economic contraction. Downbeat corporate outlooks reinforce those concerns. The two-year yield reaches 3.901% and the 10-year is at 3.470%. (paulo.trevisani@wsj.com; @ptrevisani)\par \par \uc2 0852 ET - The euro's appreciation potential against the dollar could remain limited as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  maintains its commitment to curbing inflation, Unicredit Research says. The euro has proved resilient but failed to rise materially on \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  members signalling further interest rate rises, positive Ukraine war developments and the EU proposing measures to tackle soaring energy prices, \uc2 Unicredit\b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Roberto Mialich says in a note. "For that to happen, the Fed would need to signal its intention to scale back its pace of tightening, but this looks unlikely, given the latest US [inflation] data." The Fed is likely to raise rates by 75 basis points at Wednesday's meeting and signal further rises, Mialich says. EUR/USD falls 0.4% to 0.9964. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0851 ET - European stocks drop after downbeat Asia trading and ahead of an expected lower U.S. open. The Stoxx Europe 600, DAX and CAC 40 all fall more than 1% and the FTSE 100 backtracks 0.4%, though the latter's losses are limited as sterling falls against the euro and dollar. Brent crude rises 0.8% to $91.54 a barrel. IG futures data show the Dow opening at 30651, versus Thursday's close of 30961. "Asian markets slipped further overnight, matching the gloomy U.S. mood, as investors hunker down ahead of another big U.S. rate hike next week," IG analysts write. "U.S. and European futures remain under pressure, with the warning from \uc2 FedEx\uc2  last night about further economic weakness providing another reason for caution." (philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0819 ET - Eurozone inflation was confirmed at 9.1% on year in August in the second reading, with energy and food prices contributing the largest part to the headline number despite energy prices slowing further from their peak in June, Oxford Economics' senior economist Tomas Dvorak says in a note. "There is little sign of slowing demand having any tangible effect on prices yet, although we expect demand pressures to abate more sharply as the economy enters a recession over the winter," Dvorak says. However, with supply pressures remaining rife and the continued pass-through of high commodity prices into core inflation, the risks of higher underlying inflation in the eurozone persist, the economist warns. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0708 ET - The 1.6% monthly drop in U.K. retail sales volumes in August, the largest since July 2021, adds to evidence that the country is in the early stages of a recession that is expected to last until 2Q 2023, Berenberg says. "The big downside surprise in real retail sales, excluding autos, in August may trigger further downgrades in U.K. GDP forecasts among financial market economists," Berenberg senior economist \uc2 Kallum Pickering\uc2  says in a note. The government decision to freeze consumer energy prices might soften the shock to real incomes, but is unlikely to prevent an economic downturn, Pickering says. (xavier.fontdegloria@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0657 ET - Sterling could weaken further versus the dollar in coming months given the U.K. economy's vulnerabilities, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  says. "The U.K. current account is being eroded by high energy prices and Brexit," \uc2 Citi\uc2  analysts say in a note. The "very weak" U.K. growth picture is leading to capital account inflows drying up at a time when the U.K. needs them most as evidenced by collapsing inbound mergers and acquisitions, they say. Meanwhile, fresh fiscal risks are emerging as energy support measures might be funded entirely by the issuance of \uc2 U.K. government\uc2  bonds, or gilts, they say. \uc2 Citi\uc2  expects GBP/USD to fall to 1.10 within three months. GBP/USD falls 0.6% to 1.1401, having reached a 37-and-a-half-year low of 1.1351 earlier, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2  . (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0652 ET - Many investors have had a very bearish assessment of Italian government bonds, or BTPs, ahead of the elections, therefore the bar is relative low in order for \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  , leader of the far-right Brothers of Italy, to outperform expectations, \uc2 BlueBay Asset Management\uc2  says. "This means that there is a risk of a squeeze tighter in spreads in the wake of the election, even if Italian credit fundamentals continue to look materially challenged," chief investment officer \uc2 Mark Dowding\uc2  writes in a note. BlueBay AM is "happy" adopting a flat stance for now, is more inclined to sell into strength and would be better a buyer if the 10-year BTP-Bund spread approaches 300 basis points--versus 229bps now, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2  --in the next several months. (emese.bartha@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0652 ET - The euro faces continued weakness given risks stemming from Europe's energy crisis and Italy's general election, \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  says. A colder than average European winter could send European gas prices sharply higher, \uc2 Citi\uc2  analysts say in a note. Moreover, Italy's centre-right coalition--which is leading polls ahead of the Sep. 25 election--could water down or unravel reforms conditional on EU recovery funds, they say. Tensions between the EU and the Italian government could rise, leading to similar situation to that after the 2018 election, they say. "This saw significant widening in Italian government bonds-German Bund yield spreads (100-150bps) and EUR/USD weakness (9%)." \uc2 Citi\uc2  expects EUR/USD to trade at 0.98 over the next three months, compared to 0.9976 currently. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0646 ET - Eurozone final inflation data for August confirm that price pressures are very strong and broad-based, Capital Economics' senior Europe economist Jack Allen-Reynolds says in a note. Headline inflation hit 9.1% year-on-year in August. Nearly half of eurozone inflation was directly due to oil and gas and Allen-Reynolds says energy inflation should soon start to fall sharply. However, inflation in the eurozone is about much more than just energy, he says. Core inflation reached a record high of 4.3% in August. Therefore, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will need to continue hiking interest rates aggressively at forthcoming meetings, according to the analyst. (maria.martinez@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0554 ET - The Swedish krona and Norwegian krone look set to recover as risk appetite should improve towards year-end, \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  says. Moreover, the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  is unlikely to fall behind the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in raising interest rates, providing a further boost to the SEK, \uc2 BofA\uc2  analysts say in a note. The NOK should benefit from higher oil prices, while markets "still underestimate the relative \uc2 Norges Bank\uc2  stance," having been the first G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise rates, they say. \uc2 BofA\uc2  expects EUR/NOK to fall to 9.70 and EUR/SEK to reach 10.30 by year-end. EUR/NOK rises 0.6% to 10.2280 after hitting a near 2-month high of 10.2382 earlier. EUR/SEK gains 0.2% to 10.7557. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 16, 2022 09:26 ET (13:26 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220916ei9g001jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
